!Bug reports / requests

* "ke ko'a ce ko'e ke'e ce ko'i" does not parse. â€”((kpreid))
* The parse tree for "ko'a ce ke ko'e ce ko'i ke'e" is unnecessarily hard to process, as it contains the ke/ke'e brackets in the same parent node (sumti1) as the elements of the outer list; the (somewhat postprocessed) output in TermL syntax is sumti1(sumti2, joikEk, KE, sumti, KEhE); it would be preferable for the last three elements to have a subnode to themselves. â€”((kpreid))
* Non-Lojban words in ZOI quotes yield invalid TermL: "zoi zoi $ zoi" contains innerWord( $ ) when it should be innerWord( "$" ). 'zoi zoi " zoi' is probably another useful test case. â€”((kpreid))